  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe expression {推測|すいそく}の{域|いき}を{出|で}ない (\"does not go beyond speculation\") is a set phrase used to acknowledge that something is just a guess. {推測|すいそく} is more formal than {予想|よそう} (prediction) and implies reasoning from indirect evidence.\n\nCOMPARISON WITH SIMILAR WORDS:\n- {推測|すいそく}: inference from indirect evidence; formal\n- {推定|すいてい}: estimation based on data; more technical\n- {憶測|おくそく}: speculation; often negative nuance (unfounded guessing)\n- {予想|よそう}: prediction; forward-looking, less analytical\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {推測|すいそく}の{域|いき}を{出|で}ない: to be nothing more than speculation\n- {推測|すいそく}が{当|あ}たる: one's guess proves correct\n- {推測|すいそく}にすぎない: to be merely speculation\n- ～と{推測|すいそく}される: it is speculated that ~",
